[verse 1]
Humble me, Lord, as I come unto Thee,
Deepen my trust in Thy mercy t’ward me;
Bowed with my burden of sin and of dross,
Lowly, I bend at the foot of Thy cross.

[chorus]
Let me but enter Thy wounded side,
This world rejecting, there to abide;
Only in Thee can my spirit be blest,
Low at Thy feet, Lord, find peace and rest.

[verse 2]
Humble me, Lord, as I offer my plea,
Cleanse every stain, from each sin set me free;
I am unworthy, no merit I claim;
Looking to Jesus, I trust in His name.

[chorus]
Let me but enter Thy wounded side,
This world rejecting, there to abide;
Only in Thee can my spirit be blest,
Low at Thy feet, Lord, find peace and rest.

[verse 3]
Humble me, Lord, and I then will be sure
Of perfect redemption, full and secure;
Though, often in sorrow my heart despaired,
I know my salvation now is prepared.

[chorus]
Let me but enter Thy wounded side,
This world rejecting, there to abide;
Only in Thee can my spirit be blest,
Low at Thy feet, Lord, find peace and rest.
